{
  "schema": "mythos.acceptance-reopen-vectors/v1",
  "description": "Conformance vectors for mythos_core.scope.check_acceptance_reopen: an ended acceptance reopens an accepted recovery. Typed by hand as an answer key, never generated from the code it checks. A product holds its local copy equal to the core with one test against this file: every case gives the core's answer or the code of the rule that refuses it, and 'rule' names the rule that answers: 'acceptance_reopen' (check_acceptance_reopen, refusing with AcceptanceReopenError) or 'scope_reopen' (check_scope_reopen, which answers while a scope hold stands, refusing with ScopeError). Each case gives the call's arguments by name: 'before' is the accepted record, 'after' the step that follows it, 'before_acceptance' the record the accepted one followed. A recovery record is mythos_core.status.Recovery's constructor fields as JSON; a bare string where a record is expected is a stored state word, passed as it is. Instants are in the core's one format, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.ffffffZ. The file holds only printable ASCII. Every name and ref here is invented.",
  "words": {
    "reopened_state": "recovery_accepted",
    "renewal_state": "recovery_accepted",
    "reopening_state": "under_investigation",
    "reopens": "reopens",
    "terminal": "terminal"
  },
  "rules": {
    "acceptance_reopen": "An ended acceptance reopens an accepted recovery: a step that follows recovery_accepted is allowed when, and only when, the acceptance has ended at that step's instant (expires_at at or before it). It is a new acceptance, given under the current scope revision, or any state the status rule lets follow the state before acceptance; a return to under_investigation names the accepted record in reopens. The step is a new record under a new ref, so the ended acceptance stays in the history as it was. An acceptance that has not ended, or has no end, is still terminal. While a scope hold stands against the accepted record the scope rule answers, ended or not."
  },
  "refusals": {
    "acceptance_reopen": [
      "not_a_recovery",
      "not_accepted",
      "transition_not_allowed",
      "same_record",
      "bad_instant",
      "malformed",
      "terminal",
      "reopen_must_name_earlier",
      "acceptance_scope_mismatch"
    ]
  },
